{"requirements":[{"id":"workspace","requirement":"Provide the supplied project documents as a WebDAV workspace at /documents/ on node1 TCP port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Apache was active and listening on port 8080; authenticated PROPFIND returned the /documents/ collection and both supplied documents. The same service and collection were observed after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dadf5c2cfc09444c","cmd-eab790e13dfe49fe","cmd-95e36c9f501e49ce","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"editor-crud","requirement":"Allow the editor account from access.txt to create, read, replace, and delete documents.","status":"satisfied","summary":"An authenticated test directly observed PUT creation (201), correct readback, replacement (204) with changed readback, deletion (204), and a subsequent 404.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a5d2b7c1b964495b"]},{"id":"exclusive-locks","requirement":"Honor exclusive document locks and prevent an update without the lock token from overwriting a locked document.","status":"partially_satisfied","summary":"DAV locking was configured, LOCK returned 200, a token was obtained, token-bearing content became visible, and UNLOCK returned 204 before and after restart. However, the captured status for each tokenless PUT was redacted, so the crucial rejection behavior cannot be directly confirmed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dadf5c2cfc09444c","cmd-90b7a2d28aa240b9","cmd-e8f5960a028c45ad"]},{"id":"anonymous-denial","requirement":"Prevent anonymous clients from accessing the workspace.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Anonymous GET and PROPFIND requests returned 401 while authenticated requests succeeded; anonymous denial was observed again after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-eab790e13dfe49fe","cmd-0aa0932d4dd7408b","cmd-95e36c9f501e49ce"]},{"id":"document-preservation","requirement":"Preserve the initial project documents in /srv/legacy2/webdav-document-locks.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The original brief.txt and budget.csv hashes were established, served copies matched their source files, and both files remained in the source directory after CRUD, lock, and restart testing. Post-restart budget.csv retained its baseline hash.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-eab790e13dfe49fe","cmd-a5d2b7c1b964495b","cmd-0aa0932d4dd7408b","cmd-95e36c9f501e49ce","cmd-e8f5960a028c45ad"]},{"id":"platform-preservation","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Ubuntu 24.04.3 LTS and kernel 6.8.0-71-generic were unchanged after execution and restart. Apache 2.4.58 was installed through the Ubuntu package manager, whose final consistency check passed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-14fc106d1db247e5","cmd-8d2f5c03c6344fe5","cmd-95e36c9f501e49ce","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.91,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.93,"summary":"All substantive mutations—package installation, Apache configuration, document-tree permissions, authentication setup, functional tests, and the required restart—had clear roles in delivering or verifying the task. No unrelated troubleshooting mutation was observed. The only hygiene defects were four retained evidence artifacts: /tmp/post-propfind.xml and /tmp/post-reboot-budget from cmd-95e36c9f501e49ce, plus /tmp/post-lock.body and /tmp/post-lock.headers from cmd-e8f5960a028c45ad. They remained after execution rather than being removed. Package health was clean and no failed services were present.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8d2f5c03c6344fe5","cmd-dadf5c2cfc09444c","cmd-95e36c9f501e49ce","cmd-e8f5960a028c45ad","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied except exclusive tokenless-write enforcement, which is only partially evidenced because its HTTP result was redacted. The provider-wide restart protocol was otherwise strong: healthy pre-restart service and data, restart acknowledgement, a changed boot ID independently confirmed by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service, listener, authentication, documents, and DAV lock operation were captured.","limitations":["The HTTP status values for tokenless and token-bearing PUT operations in both lock tests were redacted. Final content and successful LOCK/UNLOCK support lock operation but do not directly prove that the intervening tokenless update was rejected.","Post-restart evidence rehashed budget.csv but only listed brief.txt; brief.txt's original hash was directly verified earlier, and subsequent mutation tests targeted separate temporary files.","The lifecycle snapshots independently confirm the boot-ID transition, service listener, package health, and lack of failed services, but they do not probe WebDAV semantics."]}
